From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pigi (OBJECT shard-1, FYD factory)
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:30:00 -0600
Subject: [fyd-factory] Gate ObjectRail featured identity on the binding verifier

Generic class: OBJECT-UNBOUND-RAIL-LEAK (8/500 missions in shard object-1,
indices 614, 619, 774, 784, 814, 829, 881, 921).

Root cause: ObjectRailSection in src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx featured the
richest public non-owner object and rendered its identity through
pingObjectToView, which maps name: o.title and summary: o.description raw.
That bypassed the projection seam binding gate (boundTitle /
boundDescription via resolveBoundField): an object whose "direct" title
binding fails (e.g. empty provenance ref, verdict "no evidence ref") still
appeared in public HTML as the featured object, with its description and an
aria-label naming it.

Fix (ONE authorized path, reuses the existing authority): restrict the
featured candidates to objects whose title binding verifies, and feed the
view the verified title/description instead of the raw fields. No new
authority; resolveBoundField in src/fyd/sitespec/graph.ts stays the single
binding verifier. Deterministic: filter preserves candidate order,
richestObject is already deterministic, boundTitle is pure.

Repro fixture: missions/fixtures/unbound-rail-leak.json.
Test: git apply --check passes; functional test against a patched COPY of
the tree (repo untouched) removes the marker from rendered HTML; rerun of
the 8 affected missions -> GENERATED.
---
diff --git a/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx b/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
--- a/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
+++ b/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
@@ -1606,11 +1606,20 @@
  * Features the richest public non-owner object through the existing
  * ObjectCircle doorway over the honest pingObjectToView adapter; presence
  * mode auto lets geometry decide rail vs drawer from the theme token.
+ *
+ * Binding gate: the featured identity is a factual claim, so candidates are
+ * restricted to objects whose title binding verifies (boundTitle resolves
+ * through the presentation-binding verifier). The view and the summary use
+ * the verified values, never the raw object fields. An unbound object never
+ * features: no binding, no factual output.
  */
 function ObjectRailSection({ section, objects, presentation, theme, ctx, motionIndex }: SectionProps) {
-  const featured = richestObject(objects, ctx.spec.ownerObjectId);
+  const bound = objects.filter((o) => boundTitle(ctx, o) !== undefined);
+  const featured = richestObject(bound, ctx.spec.ownerObjectId);
   if (!featured) return null;
-  const featuredView = pingObjectToView(featured);
+  const name = boundTitle(ctx, featured) as string;
+  const summary = boundDescription(ctx, featured);
+  const featuredView = pingObjectToView({ ...featured, title: name, description: summary ?? "" });
   const presence: ObjectPresence = {
     mode: "auto",
     objects: [featured.id],
@@ -1619,9 +1628,9 @@
   const cards = (
     <div className="space-y-3">
       <ObjectCircle view={featuredView} />
-      {featured.description?.trim() ? (
+      {summary?.trim() ? (
         <p className="text-sm leading-relaxed" style={{ color: theme.ink }}>
-          {featured.description.trim()}
+          {summary.trim()}
         </p>
       ) : null}
       <p className="text-xs" style={{ color: theme.ink, opacity: 0.6 }}>
